1
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,808
♪ In the
not-too-distant future ♪

2
00:00:07,808 --> 00:00:11,145
♪ Next Sunday A.D. ♪

3
00:00:11,145 --> 00:00:14,015
♪ There was a guy named Joel ♪

4
00:00:14,015 --> 00:00:17,385
♪ Not too different
from you or me ♪

5
00:00:17,385 --> 00:00:20,222
♪ He worked at
Gizmonic Institute ♪

6
00:00:20,222 --> 00:00:23,725
♪ Just another face
in a red jumpsuit ♪

7
00:00:23,725 --> 00:00:26,493
♪ He did a good job
cleaning up the place ♪

8
00:00:26,493 --> 00:00:27,962
♪ But his bosses
didn't like him ♪

9
00:00:27,962 --> 00:00:32,967
♪ So they shot him into space ♪

10
00:00:33,868 --> 00:00:36,137
♪ We'll send him cheesy movies ♪

11
00:00:36,137 --> 00:00:38,338
♪ The worst we can find ♪

12
00:00:38,338 --> 00:00:39,673
♪ La-la-la ♪

13
00:00:39,673 --> 00:00:42,110
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all ♪

14
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:44,612
♪ And we'll monitor his mind ♪

15
00:00:44,612 --> 00:00:45,947
♪ La-la-la ♪

16
00:00:45,947 --> 00:00:48,450
♪ Now keep in mind
Joel can't control ♪

17
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:50,852
♪ Where the movies
begin or end ♪

18
00:00:50,852 --> 00:00:52,087
♪ La-la-la ♪

19
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:54,788
♪ Because he used
those special parts ♪

20
00:00:54,788 --> 00:00:58,392
♪ To make his robot friends ♪

21
00:00:59,627 --> 00:01:01,128
♪ Robot Roll Call: ♪
- All right, let's go!

22
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:02,697
♪ Cambot ♪
- Pan left!

23
00:01:02,697 --> 00:01:03,965
♪ Gypsy ♪
- Hi, girl!

24
00:01:03,965 --> 00:01:05,767
♪ Tom Servo ♪
- What a cool guy!

25
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:07,268
♪ Croooow ♪
= He's a wisecracker.

26
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:10,372
♪ If you're wondering how
he eats and breathes ♪

27
00:01:10,372 --> 00:01:12,573
♪ and other science facts ♪

28
00:01:12,573 --> 00:01:14,042
♪ La la la ♪

29
00:01:14,042 --> 00:01:16,410
♪ Then repeat to yourself,
it's just a show ♪

30
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:19,447
♪ I should really just relax ♪

31
00:01:19,447 --> 00:01:24,418
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000 ♪

32
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:25,587
(guitar twangs)

33
00:01:25,587 --> 00:01:30,525
(mechanical whirring)
(doors closing)

34
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:35,797
- Okay, Gypsy, is it?

35
00:01:35,797 --> 00:01:38,332
Okay, where are you from?

36
00:01:38,332 --> 00:01:40,735
- Uh, right here
at the satellite.

37
00:01:40,735 --> 00:01:43,437
- Uh-huh, and what do
you do for a living?

38
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:45,340
- You programmed me to do

39
00:01:45,340 --> 00:01:48,175
some of the higher
functions of the ship.

40
00:01:48,175 --> 00:01:49,577
- Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, and who
does your hair, Gypsy?

41
00:01:49,577 --> 00:01:51,312
I think that's great.

42
00:01:52,213 --> 00:01:53,180
- Bite me.

43
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:54,282
- You live around here much?

44
00:01:54,282 --> 00:01:55,883
I'm kidding of course.

45
00:01:55,883 --> 00:01:58,720
- Hi everybody, welcome
to the Satellite of Love.

46
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:01,388
A lot of you are probably
asking yourselves right now,

47
00:02:01,388 --> 00:02:03,023
what kind of a weird
tripped out scene

48
00:02:03,023 --> 00:02:04,492
is Joel into this week?

49
00:02:04,492 --> 00:02:05,227
Well, it's--

50
00:02:05,227 --> 00:02:06,060
Ow!

51
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,462
- Oh, sorry.

52
00:02:07,462 --> 00:02:10,732
Get this, this week Joel
fancies himself a caricaturist.

53
00:02:10,732 --> 00:02:12,300
Right now he's doing Gypsy.

54
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,802
For those of you who don't know,

55
00:02:13,802 --> 00:02:15,503
a caricaturist is an artist
who makes anyone he draws

56
00:02:15,503 --> 00:02:16,905
look like Jack Sue.

57
00:02:16,905 --> 00:02:17,738
Ow, ow.

58
00:02:18,940 --> 00:02:21,608
- The only problem
is, Gypsy's nude.

59
00:02:21,608 --> 00:02:23,512
- Hey, you guys are
nude too, you know.

60
00:02:23,512 --> 00:02:24,345
- What?

61
00:02:24,345 --> 00:02:25,180
- Hey, he's right!

62
00:02:25,180 --> 00:02:26,013
- Oh my god!

63
00:02:26,013 --> 00:02:26,848
- Whoa!

64
00:02:31,352 --> 00:02:32,453
- What do you think?

65
00:02:32,453 --> 00:02:33,387
- Well...

66
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:35,423
(screaming)

67
00:02:35,423 --> 00:02:36,623
(crashing)

68
00:02:36,623 --> 00:02:38,258
- Well, at least I
can draw you, Cambot,

69
00:02:38,258 --> 00:02:39,893
in the way I've
always wanted to.

70
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:42,097
Without a stitch on.

71
00:02:42,097 --> 00:02:45,667
(instrumental theme music)

72
00:02:48,135 --> 00:02:49,270
Well, what do you think?

73
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:51,038
- It's really not that good.

74
00:02:51,038 --> 00:02:52,373
I look like Garrick Utley

75
00:02:52,373 --> 00:02:54,142
with a cream pitcher
wedged in his skull.

76
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:56,410
- Well yours is pretty
good, isn't it Tom?

77
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:57,912
- Yeah, right.

78
00:02:57,912 --> 00:02:59,680
Wouldn't pick up my worst
enemy's dog droppings

79
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,015
with this piece of crap.

80
00:03:01,015 --> 00:03:02,950
Oh, but I'm sure
you'll get better.

81
00:03:02,950 --> 00:03:07,022
Uh-oh, Dum-dum and
Stinkypants are calling there.

82
00:03:07,022 --> 00:03:07,955
(chuckling)

83
00:03:07,955 --> 00:03:09,323
- Dum-dum and Stinkypants,

84
00:03:09,323 --> 00:03:10,758
where do they come
up with this stuff?

85
00:03:10,758 --> 00:03:11,893
(chuckling)

86
00:03:11,893 --> 00:03:13,828
Oh, I love that little red guy.

87
00:03:13,828 --> 00:03:15,963
Oh look at me, I'm
a little red robot

88
00:03:15,963 --> 00:03:18,398
and I can't move my arms.

89
00:03:18,398 --> 00:03:19,900
- Frank.
- Huh?

90
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,035
- Why don't you ask them to do

91
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:23,037
their Invention Exchange, okay?

92
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:25,138
- Look, I love to laugh
and we're having fun,

93
00:03:25,138 --> 00:03:28,910
but please, can we get to
the Invention Exchange?

94
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:31,578
(chuckling) Stinkypants.

95
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:33,882
- Well sirs, our Invention
Exchange this week

96
00:03:33,882 --> 00:03:36,183
is based on those
beer can caddy hats

97
00:03:36,183 --> 00:03:39,120
thatúshirtless obnoxious
guys wear at baseball games.

98
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,622
- Yeah, only ours are built for

99
00:03:40,622 --> 00:03:43,157
whisper-thin, musky
bohemian types.

100
00:03:43,157 --> 00:03:45,427
- Yeah. They're called
the Big Gulp Berets.

101
00:03:45,427 --> 00:03:48,095
As you can see, they've
got caddies on the side

102
00:03:48,095 --> 00:03:51,165
to hold your favorite
ice cold Evian or Volvic

103
00:03:51,165 --> 00:03:53,668
or any other criminally
priced spring water.

104
00:03:53,668 --> 00:03:56,470
- Now when you go see the
Bloody Unicorn Puppet Theater's

105
00:03:56,470 --> 00:03:59,140
production of Marat Sade, you
can still have your hands free

106
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:02,143
to scribble poetry or
dab on patchouli oil.

107
00:04:02,143 --> 00:04:04,812
- And at the dank uptown
cast party afterwards,

108
00:04:04,812 --> 00:04:09,617
when the check comes, it frees
up your hands to discover...

109
00:04:09,617 --> 00:04:11,885
- I must have left my
money in my other pants.

110
00:04:11,885 --> 00:04:13,788
Could you spot me tonight?

111
00:04:13,788 --> 00:04:14,988
What do you think, sirs?

112
00:04:14,988 --> 00:04:17,058
- Very amusing, Joel,
but I don't cotton

113
00:04:17,058 --> 00:04:19,660
to those long-haired
artsy types.

114
00:04:19,660 --> 00:04:24,498
Now, you little scamps beg me
to do the Invention Exchange.

115
00:04:24,498 --> 00:04:26,533
- (laughing) Okay, sirs.

116
00:04:26,533 --> 00:04:29,437
Please do the
Invention Exchange.

117
00:04:29,437 --> 00:04:30,270
- No.

118
00:04:31,605 --> 00:04:32,540
Well, okay.

119
00:04:34,242 --> 00:04:37,512
As a scientist, I'm constantly
working with materials

120
00:04:37,512 --> 00:04:40,213
that threaten life
on a global scale,

121
00:04:40,213 --> 00:04:42,750
and sometimes they spill.

122
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:46,887
Enter these polysorbent
biohazard clean-up pillows.

123
00:04:46,887 --> 00:04:50,023
Once used only for
industry, we've brought them

124
00:04:50,023 --> 00:04:55,028
into the home with
our new designer
biohaZard throw pillows.

125
00:04:56,497 --> 00:04:59,733
Now Frank has prepared
a little one-act play

126
00:04:59,733 --> 00:05:01,902
to explain their efficacy.

127
00:05:08,608 --> 00:05:11,512
- Well, enough
Charles in Charge.

128
00:05:11,512 --> 00:05:14,115
I'd better get to
work on that hardy new

129
00:05:14,115 --> 00:05:17,718
strain of dysentery
I've been mutating.

130
00:05:17,718 --> 00:05:19,120
Oh, no!

131
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,722
Not again!

132
00:05:20,722 --> 00:05:25,627
Well, Dr. Forrester's decorator
biohazard clean-up pillows,

133
00:05:27,895 --> 00:05:28,730
I'm saved!

134
00:05:30,097 --> 00:05:32,933
Dr. Clayton
Forrester, I love you.

135
00:05:34,535 --> 00:05:36,803
(clapping)

136
00:05:38,472 --> 00:05:41,108
- Well Jimmy Smits,
your movie today

137
00:05:41,108 --> 00:05:44,045
is roasted fresh from the
kitchens of Bert I. Gordon.

138
00:05:44,045 --> 00:05:46,080
It's a fetid little
piece of tripe

139
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:49,850
featuring sword and
sorcery and Gary Lockwood

140
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,553
and an embarrassed
Basil Rathbone.

141
00:05:52,553 --> 00:05:54,955
It's called The Magic Sword.

142
00:05:54,955 --> 00:05:59,827
- Doctor, I think I sucked up
some of that hazardous stuff.

143
00:06:02,197 --> 00:06:04,532
- Oh, don't be a baby, I've
taken gallons of that stuff

144
00:06:04,532 --> 00:06:07,033
and it's only made me
stronger and taller.

145
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:09,337
- But I don't feel good.

146
00:06:09,337 --> 00:06:11,572
- Oh what are you
gonna do now, cry, huh?

147
00:06:11,572 --> 00:06:13,173
You gonna cry, baby, huh?

148
00:06:13,173 --> 00:06:14,375
You gonna cry?

149
00:06:14,375 --> 00:06:15,643
One, two, three, cry.

150
00:06:15,643 --> 00:06:16,510
(alarms blaring)

151
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:17,878
- Oh, we got movie sign!

152
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:20,047
(all yelling)

153
00:06:20,047 --> 00:06:23,217
(mechanical whirring)

154
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:37,498
- [Tom] Say, Bert I.
Gordon's gone color!

155
00:06:37,498 --> 00:06:41,968
- [Joel] Can slice a tomato so
thin you can see through it.

156
00:06:41,968 --> 00:06:44,505
(dramatic music)

157
00:06:44,505 --> 00:06:49,510
- [Crow] Ah, I'll have Basil
Rathbone with pesto, please.

158
00:06:50,377 --> 00:06:52,113
- [Joel] Give her a higher love.

159
00:06:52,113 --> 00:06:55,850
- [Crow] Even then
she was really old.

160
00:06:55,850 --> 00:06:57,017
- [Tom] Oh, you know,
I love Dean Martin

161
00:06:57,017 --> 00:07:00,220
in those old Anne Helm movies.

162
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,523
- [Joel] Oh, it's Matt Helm.

163
00:07:03,657 --> 00:07:06,927
Oh, Merritt Stone,
that's my birthstone.

164
00:07:08,863 --> 00:07:10,665
- [Crow] Callahan,
it was Callahan.

165
00:07:10,665 --> 00:07:13,500
Marlene Callahan,
she was the one.

166
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,537
- [Joel] Nick, Paul
and Jon Bon Tempi.

167
00:07:16,537 --> 00:07:19,907
- [Crow] Is a woman who hangs
out with hags a hag hag?

168
00:07:19,907 --> 00:07:21,142
- [Joel] No...

169
00:07:21,142 --> 00:07:23,210
- [Tom] Makes ya
think, doesn't it?

170
00:07:23,210 --> 00:07:26,047
Uh-oh, we're in
big trouble, guys.

171
00:07:27,682 --> 00:07:29,783
- [Joel] We are in
really big trouble.

172
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:31,218
- [Tom] Yep, yep.

173
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:35,255
(Tom humming along with music)

174
00:07:35,255 --> 00:07:39,893
- [Crow] Music made under
strict rabbinical supervision.

175
00:07:47,468 --> 00:07:51,638
- [Tom] Dragon trainer,
they're kidding us, right?

176
00:07:54,042 --> 00:07:58,712
- [Crow] This isn't a movie,
it's an employment program!

177
00:08:00,447 --> 00:08:01,848
- [Tom] Isn't that what
they call you, girl?

178
00:08:01,848 --> 00:08:03,683
Whadda they call you
up there in wardrobe?

179
00:08:03,683 --> 00:08:07,322
- [Joel] They call
me Esther Krebs.

180
00:08:07,322 --> 00:08:10,858
- [Tom] We are in deep,
deep trouble, guys.

181
00:08:14,595 --> 00:08:16,997
And yes, you can be too thin.

182
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:21,702
- [All] Say...

183
00:08:21,702 --> 00:08:22,570
Aaah!

184
00:08:22,570 --> 00:08:23,905
- [Crow] Well...

185
00:08:23,905 --> 00:08:26,007
- He left home hours ago.

186
00:08:28,475 --> 00:08:29,543
- [Joel] Oh, that's so creative.

187
00:08:29,543 --> 00:08:31,112
She has a little
cafe down there.

188
00:08:31,112 --> 00:08:35,550
- What good is my sorcery
if I can't help my own boy?

189
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:38,018
Answer me, someone!

190
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,553
- [Crow] Roddy McDowell, no!

191
00:08:39,553 --> 00:08:41,388
- He's not fooling me.

192
00:08:42,257 --> 00:08:44,458
I know where he is.

193
00:08:44,458 --> 00:08:47,060
He's at the magic pool again.

194
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,897
♪ A double pleasure's
waiting for you ♪

195
00:08:49,897 --> 00:08:50,832
- He is in love.

196
00:08:50,832 --> 00:08:52,233
- You think I don't know it?

197
00:08:52,233 --> 00:08:54,068
I've tried to cure him of it.

198
00:08:54,068 --> 00:08:56,503
Am I losing my skill
as a sorceress?

199
00:08:56,503 --> 00:08:59,507
- [Tom] Among other things.

200
00:08:59,507 --> 00:09:00,742
- No, no Sybil.

201
00:09:02,108 --> 00:09:03,677
- [Crow] Oh, that's
calling the kettle black.

202
00:09:03,677 --> 00:09:06,847
- To cure snakebite,
chillblains,

203
00:09:06,847 --> 00:09:09,950
carbuncles, pinkeye, hangnails--

204
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:11,718
- [Joel] Hello, Mata.

205
00:09:12,753 --> 00:09:14,188
- Yes, yes Sybil.

206
00:09:15,923 --> 00:09:20,093
- Then why can't I rid the
boy of this, this fever?

207
00:09:20,093 --> 00:09:21,528
- George is a man.

208
00:09:21,528 --> 00:09:23,430
- [Tom] She hired two
brown-nosers to hang around.

209
00:09:23,430 --> 00:09:26,133
- Human, yes, but hardly a man.

210
00:09:26,133 --> 00:09:28,402
He's a mere boy of 20.

211
00:09:28,402 --> 00:09:29,337
- In love.

212
00:09:29,337 --> 00:09:31,472
- [Crow] You guys really bug me.

213
00:09:31,472 --> 00:09:34,208
- George, already
a man, in love.

214
00:09:38,478 --> 00:09:41,182
He ought to be at home
learning a good trade.

215
00:09:41,182 --> 00:09:46,020
- [Joel] Like computer science,
refrigeration, gun repair.

216
00:09:47,788 --> 00:09:50,658
- [Tom] Now is that
BJ or the Bear?

217
00:09:51,792 --> 00:09:54,028
(Joel imitates vomiting)

218
00:09:54,028 --> 00:09:54,895
- Pool of magic--

219
00:09:54,895 --> 00:09:55,730
- [Crow] What?

220
00:09:55,730 --> 00:09:56,763
- Obey my wish.

221
00:09:56,763 --> 00:09:58,465
Bring her vision into my sight.

222
00:09:58,465 --> 00:10:00,935
That's right, that's right.

223
00:10:00,935 --> 00:10:04,272
- [Joel] Answer unclear,
ask again later.

224
00:10:04,272 --> 00:10:06,107
- She's at the palace.

225
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:12,713
♪ It's the undersea kingdom,
for you and for me ♪

226
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,548
- Perhaps the throne room.

227
00:10:15,548 --> 00:10:18,052
- [Joel] Calgon, take me away.

228
00:10:19,187 --> 00:10:21,955
- [Crow] It's King Grady!

229
00:10:21,955 --> 00:10:24,458
- [Joel] Oh, not another
Jane Fonda video.

230
00:10:24,458 --> 00:10:27,428
(exotic music)

231
00:10:27,428 --> 00:10:29,130
Imogene Coca, no!

232
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:30,932
- [Tom] Imogene Coca, yes.

233
00:10:30,932 --> 00:10:34,168
Talk about your show of shows.

234
00:10:34,168 --> 00:10:35,502
- [Crow] I hate
it when they hire

235
00:10:35,502 --> 00:10:38,738
these strip-o-grams
for my birthday.

236
00:10:38,738 --> 00:10:41,642
- Try the, try the sunken garden

237
00:10:41,642 --> 00:10:43,543
in the palace by
the oriental pool.

238
00:10:43,543 --> 00:10:46,913
- [Joel] Have breakfast
with me. (burbling)

239
00:10:46,913 --> 00:10:49,150
- [Crow] Ah, somebody flushed.

240
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,718
- That's right, there she is.

241
00:10:51,718 --> 00:10:54,688
- [Tom] Oh I get
it, he's got cable.

242
00:10:57,023 --> 00:10:58,258
- There she is.

243
00:11:00,193 --> 00:11:01,395
- [Crow] It's Fanny Fox.

244
00:11:01,395 --> 00:11:02,697
- [Tom] It's a Maxfield
Parrish painting.

245
00:11:02,697 --> 00:11:03,963
- [Joel] You're both
right, it's Fanny Fox

246
00:11:03,963 --> 00:11:05,800
in a Maxfield Parrish painting.

247
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:09,570
Both jokes can work
together, let's watch on.

248
00:11:12,305 --> 00:11:13,407
- [Tom] Hey mom, hey
mom, watch me mom,

249
00:11:13,407 --> 00:11:14,408
watch me, watch this.

250
00:11:14,408 --> 00:11:15,910
(burbling)

251
00:11:15,910 --> 00:11:19,747
- [Crow] Gidget goes to
the Renaissance Festival.

252
00:11:21,648 --> 00:11:23,650
- [Tom] That's
precise editing, huh?

253
00:11:23,650 --> 00:11:25,318
- No, I'm just as
furious as ever.

254
00:11:25,318 --> 00:11:28,288
- [Joel] I am furious yellow.

255
00:11:28,288 --> 00:11:30,257
- You can do
whatever you please.

256
00:11:30,257 --> 00:11:32,660
Fall in love, fall
out of it again.

257
00:11:32,660 --> 00:11:34,828
A squire one day, a
stableboy the next.

258
00:11:34,828 --> 00:11:36,063
- [Crow] I get the
point, all right!

259
00:11:36,063 --> 00:11:36,897
Geez.

260
00:11:37,765 --> 00:11:39,600
- I can't even speak to a man,

261
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,302
let alone have him look at me.

262
00:11:42,302 --> 00:11:44,938
- That's the penalty
of being a princess.

263
00:11:44,938 --> 00:11:47,073
- But even a princess
should be allowed romance.

264
00:11:47,073 --> 00:11:48,742
- [Tom] Even cowgirls
get the blues.

265
00:11:48,742 --> 00:11:50,377
- How will I ever meet him?

266
00:11:50,377 --> 00:11:51,912
- [Girl] Who, my lady?

267
00:11:51,912 --> 00:11:54,148
- One I could love.

268
00:11:54,148 --> 00:11:55,448
- [Crow] Think that's
her natural color?

269
00:11:55,448 --> 00:11:58,485
- [Joel] She has been
hitting the dye pot.

270
00:11:58,485 --> 00:11:59,687
- But your gown.

271
00:11:59,687 --> 00:12:01,388
- [Princess] I'll dress myself.

272
00:12:01,388 --> 00:12:02,823
- Well then what will you do?

273
00:12:02,823 --> 00:12:05,425
- Oh, what I always
do, sit here and dream.

274
00:12:05,425 --> 00:12:07,828
- [Joel] Sit there and drink?

275
00:12:10,530 --> 00:12:12,500
- [Woman] Princess Helene.

276
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,735
- [Tom] Your lights are on.

277
00:12:17,103 --> 00:12:18,338
- Who are you?

278
00:12:18,338 --> 00:12:21,375
- [Joel] Just came to
freak you out, baby.

279
00:12:21,375 --> 00:12:23,443
- What do you want?

280
00:12:23,443 --> 00:12:24,578
- [Joel] This doesn't
do anything for you?

281
00:12:24,578 --> 00:12:26,080
Come on, I'm a ghost.

282
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,515
- Stay away!

283
00:12:27,515 --> 00:12:29,450
- [Crow] Marcia Wallace!

284
00:12:29,450 --> 00:12:31,152
- Don't you come any closer.

285
00:12:31,152 --> 00:12:34,988
- No, Princess, I'm going
to take care of you.

286
00:12:36,957 --> 00:12:38,192
- [Tom] She's stuck!

287
00:12:38,192 --> 00:12:40,293
Bang her on the side
of the head there.

288
00:12:40,293 --> 00:12:42,963
- [Crow] 2,000 flushes.

289
00:12:42,963 --> 00:12:44,398
- Helene!

290
00:12:44,398 --> 00:12:45,432
- [Tom] Delay?

291
00:12:45,432 --> 00:12:46,500
- [Joel] It's Gary Lockwood.

292
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:47,668
- [Tom] It is.

293
00:12:48,835 --> 00:12:49,770
- [Joel] Check this out.

294
00:12:49,770 --> 00:12:51,305
Open the pod bay doors, Hal.

295
00:12:51,305 --> 00:12:52,172
(giggling)
- [Tom] Good one.

296
00:12:52,172 --> 00:12:53,640
- [Crow] 'Cause it's...

297
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,075
- [Tom] Mommy, mommy, mommy,

298
00:12:55,075 --> 00:12:57,277
there was a scary
flashing thing, and it...

299
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:58,778
- Sybil, where are you!?

300
00:12:58,778 --> 00:13:00,513
- You needn't shout, George.

301
00:13:00,513 --> 00:13:01,815
- [Joel] Endora.

302
00:13:02,983 --> 00:13:04,918
- I must leave here,
she's in danger.

303
00:13:04,918 --> 00:13:07,888
- Who in the netherworld
are you talking about?

304
00:13:07,888 --> 00:13:09,088
- Princess Helene.

305
00:13:09,088 --> 00:13:10,723
I loved her from the
first moment I saw her.

306
00:13:10,723 --> 00:13:12,158
(laughing)

307
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:14,228
- A reflection in the
water and you fall in love,

308
00:13:14,228 --> 00:13:15,728
you silly child.

309
00:13:15,728 --> 00:13:18,132
- [Crow] Last week, it
was a deck of cards.

310
00:13:18,132 --> 00:13:21,368
- Let me see what
you're talking about.

311
00:13:23,237 --> 00:13:26,673
Magic mirror, show me
what has upset my boy.

312
00:13:26,673 --> 00:13:29,443
- [Crow] Adolescence,
puberty, raging hormones.

313
00:13:29,443 --> 00:13:31,145
- The princess is
gone, your majesty.

314
00:13:31,145 --> 00:13:32,780
She's not in her quarters,
not in the garden,

315
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:35,282
not by the pool, yet no one
saw her leave the palace.

316
00:13:35,282 --> 00:13:39,187
- [Tom] Well, she
works late on Tuesdays.

317
00:13:39,187 --> 00:13:40,453
- We have done that, my liege.

318
00:13:40,453 --> 00:13:42,022
Until she is found, no
one will be permitted

319
00:13:42,022 --> 00:13:43,457
in or out of the palace.

320
00:13:43,457 --> 00:13:44,958
- [Joel] He's wearing
fighting alignment.

321
00:13:44,958 --> 00:13:47,628
(trumpet music)

322
00:13:48,728 --> 00:13:49,530
- [Crow] Can't you
just walk into the room

323
00:13:49,530 --> 00:13:50,998
without a big to-do?

324
00:13:50,998 --> 00:13:52,833
- [Tom] To-do!

325
00:13:52,833 --> 00:13:55,202
- [Joel] He played
Sherlock Holmes, that one.

326
00:13:55,202 --> 00:13:56,470
- Who is this?

327
00:13:56,470 --> 00:13:57,638
- We found him skulking within

328
00:13:57,638 --> 00:13:59,240
the eastern cluster, my liege.

329
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:03,410
- [Tom] I wasn't skulking,
I was hanging around.

330
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:05,880
(thunder rumbling)

331
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,782
- [Crow] Oh no, not a solo!

332
00:14:07,782 --> 00:14:08,615
- Branton.

333
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,220
- Your most serene majesty,

334
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:15,155
you can call off the search.

335
00:14:15,155 --> 00:14:17,792
The princess, your
daughter, is in my castle,

336
00:14:17,792 --> 00:14:18,992
under lock and key.

337
00:14:18,992 --> 00:14:21,262
- [Tom] Well, as long
as she's sa-- Hey!

338
00:14:21,262 --> 00:14:22,597
- Lodac.

339
00:14:22,597 --> 00:14:24,197
- The sorcerer.

340
00:14:24,197 --> 00:14:25,933
- [Joel] No, the
pre-emergent tank mix,

341
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:28,135
of course it's the sorcerer!

342
00:14:28,135 --> 00:14:33,140
- Lodac, you say my daughter
is at your castle, but why?

343
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:34,975
How have I hurt you?

344
00:14:34,975 --> 00:14:36,677
Why have you done this thing?

345
00:14:36,677 --> 00:14:38,712
- The answer is very simple.

346
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:41,982
Your father executed my
sister for witchcraft

347
00:14:41,982 --> 00:14:44,017
when she was only 18 years old.

348
00:14:44,017 --> 00:14:47,453
I have waited until your
daughter reached that age

349
00:14:47,453 --> 00:14:52,125
so that my dragons could relish
the flesh of the princess.

350
00:14:52,125 --> 00:14:53,293
- [Joel] Oh wow.

351
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:54,262
- I beseech you.

352
00:14:54,262 --> 00:14:55,195
- Beseech nothing.

353
00:14:55,195 --> 00:14:57,097
- [Tom] Ah, beseech this.

354
00:14:57,097 --> 00:15:00,033
- [Branton] You'd have this
worm-eaten sorcerer frighten us.

355
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:01,202
- [King] Be careful, Branton.

356
00:15:01,202 --> 00:15:02,568
- Not I.

357
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:03,437
Lodac--

358
00:15:03,437 --> 00:15:04,938
- [Joel] You're a jerk.

359
00:15:04,938 --> 00:15:06,273
- I shall find your
castle, free the princess

360
00:15:06,273 --> 00:15:07,642
and see you destroyed.

361
00:15:07,642 --> 00:15:09,510
- [Crow] All while
balancing an egg on a spoon.

362
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:11,312
- Finding my castle
is no great task.

363
00:15:11,312 --> 00:15:13,047
- [Tom] Hey, MC Light
wants her necklace back.

364
00:15:13,047 --> 00:15:17,083
- You simply follow the
yellow star up north.

365
00:15:17,083 --> 00:15:20,087
The trick is how
to get there alive.

366
00:15:21,688 --> 00:15:23,223
- I shall.

367
00:15:23,223 --> 00:15:24,123
- I'm afraid not.

368
00:15:24,123 --> 00:15:27,695
(instrumental theme music)

369
00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:32,298
(thunder rumbles)

370
00:15:32,298 --> 00:15:35,135
- [Tom] Uh, Houston, we
have lift-off, roger.

371
00:15:35,135 --> 00:15:38,905
- That I shall be in
this castle of mine.

372
00:15:38,905 --> 00:15:40,307
- [Crow] He's got
a reverb pedal.

373
00:15:40,307 --> 00:15:42,777
- Who dares to
dart through this.

374
00:15:42,777 --> 00:15:44,978
(thunder rumbles)

375
00:15:44,978 --> 00:15:49,417
Let no man face my seven curses
and reach the dragon's lair.

376
00:15:49,417 --> 00:15:53,287
- [Joel] You ain't woman
enough to take my man.

377
00:15:53,287 --> 00:15:55,422
- Your curses won't stop me.

378
00:15:55,422 --> 00:15:58,025
- [Tom] Femme for
all seasons here.

379
00:15:58,025 --> 00:15:59,258
- The Princess Helene will make

380
00:15:59,258 --> 00:16:01,028
a delicate dish for my dragon.

381
00:16:01,028 --> 00:16:03,330
- [Crow] I'm serving her
over rice with fava beans.

382
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:05,065
(imitating Hannibal Lecter)

383
00:16:05,065 --> 00:16:07,633
- And now, if you'll excuse me.

384
00:16:08,835 --> 00:16:11,272
- [Tom] Uh, was that
seven days starting now,

385
00:16:11,272 --> 00:16:12,438
or is it seven days start--

386
00:16:12,438 --> 00:16:14,442
- [Crow] Aaah-aaah-aaah.

387
00:16:16,043 --> 00:16:17,778
Nevermore, nevermore!

388
00:16:19,212 --> 00:16:20,847
- [Tom] Well, suppose that
could have gone better.

389
00:16:20,847 --> 00:16:23,450
- Sir Branton, my
daughter will die.

390
00:16:23,450 --> 00:16:26,487
- No, Sire, for I
will rescue her.

391
00:16:26,487 --> 00:16:28,322
- You'll risk the seven curses?

392
00:16:28,322 --> 00:16:30,923
- [Crow] (chuckling) I
love that Carlin bit.

393
00:16:30,923 --> 00:16:34,362
- The man who saves Helene
will have her hand in marriage

394
00:16:34,362 --> 00:16:35,862
and half my kingdom.

395
00:16:35,862 --> 00:16:37,130
- [Joel] Check it out, she
looks like Ronald McDonald.

396
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:39,600
- [Crow] No one's
supposed to know.

397
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:41,135
- No, no, it is I who
must save the princess,

398
00:16:41,135 --> 00:16:42,202
not Sir Branton!

399
00:16:42,202 --> 00:16:44,203
(Tom repeating mockingly)

400
00:16:44,203 --> 00:16:46,707
- Do you think I'd let
you face Lodac's sorcery?

401
00:16:46,707 --> 00:16:49,042
- [Joel] You don't have
your learner's permit.

402
00:16:49,042 --> 00:16:51,112
- 300 years ago my
father and brother

403
00:16:51,112 --> 00:16:53,613
were devoured by Lodac's dragon.

404
00:16:53,613 --> 00:16:55,015
- [Crow] Not this story again.

405
00:16:55,015 --> 00:16:57,752
- They were great sorcerers
in their own right.

406
00:16:57,752 --> 00:17:00,220
- [Tom] I remember it
like it was 200 years ago.

407
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:02,757
- I am no match for
Lodac, I confess it.

408
00:17:02,757 --> 00:17:04,492
- [Joel] Okay, okay!

409
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,260
- But Sybil--

410
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:08,462
- [Tom] Please, I
gesticulate you!

411
00:17:08,462 --> 00:17:10,830
- Stay right here at
home where you are safe.

412
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:12,332
- [Joel] You're grounded.

413
00:17:12,332 --> 00:17:15,268
- You can have anything you
want, but you're staying here.

414
00:17:15,268 --> 00:17:17,703
- All I want is my freedom so
I can save the girl I love!

415
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,940
- [Tom] All I want is
what's coming to me!

416
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:22,475
- But you wouldn't understand
that, not being mortal!

417
00:17:22,475 --> 00:17:23,577
- [Crow] Oh, that hurt.

418
00:17:23,577 --> 00:17:25,845
- I've tried to do my best.

419
00:17:26,980 --> 00:17:28,948
- Oh, I know you have, Sybil.

420
00:17:28,948 --> 00:17:30,783
- [Sybil] Can't
you call me Mother?

421
00:17:30,783 --> 00:17:33,953
- [Joel] Oh, is it Mother today?

422
00:17:33,953 --> 00:17:35,288
- Sorry, Mother.

423
00:17:36,157 --> 00:17:38,025
- You were only a week old

424
00:17:38,025 --> 00:17:40,827
when your royal parents
died from the plague.

425
00:17:40,827 --> 00:17:42,095
- [Tom] Those were
happier times.

426
00:17:42,095 --> 00:17:44,798
- I found you, reared
you as my own son.

427
00:17:44,798 --> 00:17:47,935
- [Crow] Must have the
answers written on his hand.

428
00:17:47,935 --> 00:17:49,803
- And I'd do anything for you,

429
00:17:49,803 --> 00:17:52,305
but I can't stay here
with you anymore.

430
00:17:52,305 --> 00:17:53,973
- [Joel] It's weird!

431
00:17:55,175 --> 00:17:58,878
- I'm not a child, I'm
20 and I love Helene.

432
00:17:58,878 --> 00:18:02,248
- Talk to me of love
when you're 420.

433
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,483
- When you're human,
20 is old enough

434
00:18:03,483 --> 00:18:05,518
to feel love and misery.

435
00:18:05,518 --> 00:18:06,787
And give me my freedom.

436
00:18:06,787 --> 00:18:08,422
- [Joel] Okay, but
it's not wrapped.

437
00:18:08,422 --> 00:18:11,558
- You're being very
difficult tonight.

438
00:18:12,492 --> 00:18:14,828
Oh well, boys will be boys.

439
00:18:14,828 --> 00:18:15,762
- [Crow] In the hood.

440
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:18,532
- We'll have to cheer you up.

441
00:18:18,532 --> 00:18:20,100
Watch Mother now.

442
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:22,468
(Crow imitates cracking)

443
00:18:22,468 --> 00:18:24,805
- [Joel] I'm gonna have
a big bowl of Quisp.

444
00:18:24,805 --> 00:18:27,407
- [Crow] Get that
lady a saucer of milk.

445
00:18:27,407 --> 00:18:28,575
(Tom growls)

446
00:18:28,575 --> 00:18:31,312
- Not that trick again.

447
00:18:31,312 --> 00:18:32,578
- [Crow] Again?

448
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:35,982
Does he have a cotton
panel in those briefs?

449
00:18:35,982 --> 00:18:37,650
- George.
- [Tom] Don't ya know me?

450
00:18:37,650 --> 00:18:39,987
- I've never seen
you like this before.

451
00:18:39,987 --> 00:18:44,892
Look, if you'll cheer up, forget
about that girl and Lodac,

452
00:18:44,892 --> 00:18:47,862
I'll let you see the
presents I've chosen for you

453
00:18:47,862 --> 00:18:49,162
when you're 21.

454
00:18:49,162 --> 00:18:51,165
- [Joel] A new codpiece?

455
00:18:52,598 --> 00:18:54,735
- What sort of presents, Mother?

456
00:18:54,735 --> 00:18:56,002
- Come along.

457
00:18:56,002 --> 00:18:57,603
♪ It's Alexander's
ragtime band ♪

458
00:18:57,603 --> 00:18:59,707
- I'll show you.

459
00:18:59,707 --> 00:19:02,808
- [Tom] Packed with peanuts,
Estelle really satisfies.

460
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,778
- [Crow] Oh, yes.

461
00:19:04,778 --> 00:19:05,812
- [Tom] Crow.

462
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:10,183
(Tom humming)

463
00:19:17,623 --> 00:19:21,862
- [Joel] Why do you seek
the living among the dead?

464
00:19:23,230 --> 00:19:26,065
- [Tom] Carol Merrill,
what's behind that curtain?

465
00:19:26,065 --> 00:19:27,467
It's a new horse!

466
00:19:27,467 --> 00:19:31,137
(imitating cheering)

467
00:19:31,137 --> 00:19:32,372
- You like him?

468
00:19:32,372 --> 00:19:34,240
- [Joel] Geez, any
kid would, he's swell!

469
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:36,443
- He's magnificent.

470
00:19:36,443 --> 00:19:40,713
- [Sybil] He's yours when
you're 21, his name is Beyard.

471
00:19:40,713 --> 00:19:42,215
He's no ordinary animal.

472
00:19:42,215 --> 00:19:44,250
- [Crow] He's your father.

473
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:46,487
- [Sybil] This is the fastest
horse in all the world.

474
00:19:46,487 --> 00:19:50,823
♪ I am Mister Edgar Winter ♪

475
00:19:50,823 --> 00:19:55,662
- [Tom] And it can all be
yours if the price is right.

476
00:19:55,662 --> 00:19:56,597
- [Joel] Take the door!

477
00:19:56,597 --> 00:19:57,797
- [Crow] Go for the curtain!

478
00:19:57,797 --> 00:19:59,298
- [Tom] Curtain, curtain!

479
00:19:59,298 --> 00:20:00,133
Oh.

480
00:20:00,133 --> 00:20:01,568
(giggling)

481
00:20:01,568 --> 00:20:04,370
- [Joel] A candy striper's
outfit, thanks Mom!

482
00:20:04,370 --> 00:20:05,838
- See this?

483
00:20:05,838 --> 00:20:07,607
You'll wear it when
you ride the stallion.

484
00:20:07,607 --> 00:20:09,342
- [Crow] Used to
be your sister's.

485
00:20:09,342 --> 00:20:11,478
- Does this armor
possess magic too?

486
00:20:11,478 --> 00:20:13,380
- No weapon can pierce it.

487
00:20:13,380 --> 00:20:15,015
- [Tom] 'Cept a butter knife.

488
00:20:15,015 --> 00:20:17,750
- And this is
Ascalon, the blade.

489
00:20:19,152 --> 00:20:20,920
None like it since
the world began,

490
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,388
it defies all swords--

491
00:20:22,388 --> 00:20:24,625
- [Joel] It's a Ginsu 2000.

492
00:20:26,627 --> 00:20:30,030
- So there, all
yours when you're 21.

493
00:20:30,030 --> 00:20:31,163
- [Tom] If the price is right.

494
00:20:31,163 --> 00:20:32,432
- I'll let you go after Lodac

495
00:20:32,432 --> 00:20:35,802
for my revenge as
well as your own.

496
00:20:35,802 --> 00:20:36,803
- With the help of their magic,

497
00:20:36,803 --> 00:20:38,572
I could save the princess now.

498
00:20:38,572 --> 00:20:40,607
- No, you're not old enough.

499
00:20:40,607 --> 00:20:43,243
You wouldn't know
how to use them.

500
00:20:43,243 --> 00:20:44,745
- [Joel] No, don't touch it.

501
00:20:44,745 --> 00:20:46,380
Don't even look at it.

502
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,515
- Just to get the feeling.

503
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:50,417
Just for a while.

504
00:20:50,417 --> 00:20:51,785
(chuckling)

505
00:20:51,785 --> 00:20:52,752
- Very well.

506
00:20:58,225 --> 00:20:59,960
- Feels like a part
of my own body.

507
00:20:59,960 --> 00:21:01,728
- [Crow] So it's like your arm?

508
00:21:01,728 --> 00:21:03,130
- I feel stronger.

509
00:21:03,130 --> 00:21:04,698
- [Tom] More
confident, dry, secure.

510
00:21:04,698 --> 00:21:08,635
- It pleases me to show
you something else tonight.

511
00:21:08,635 --> 00:21:11,905
- [Joel] Boss, it's
a Hank Aaron model.

512
00:21:15,275 --> 00:21:16,208
- Who are they?

513
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:17,610
- [Crow] The Village People!

514
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:20,580
- [Sybil] The six most
valiant knights in the world.

515
00:21:20,580 --> 00:21:22,448
- [Joel] That's him,
Officer, third from the left.

516
00:21:22,448 --> 00:21:24,183
- [George] That's
real black magic.

517
00:21:24,183 --> 00:21:25,718
- I wish I could
take the credit.

518
00:21:25,718 --> 00:21:28,855
I've never been as good as
that, no, it was my brother.

519
00:21:28,855 --> 00:21:31,057
- [Tom] Geez Mom, all
this stuff was in my room

520
00:21:31,057 --> 00:21:32,725
and I never noticed it before!

521
00:21:32,725 --> 00:21:34,260
- Just great.

522
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:35,795
- [Joel] Now I can be the prep
cook I always wanted to be~

523
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:38,532
(sword clanging)

524
00:21:41,368 --> 00:21:44,637
- [Tom] Oh now I've
done it, sorry Mom.

525
00:21:46,940 --> 00:21:48,075
- Did the sword do that?

526
00:21:48,075 --> 00:21:49,342
- [Crow] Sure did, Jethro.

527
00:21:49,342 --> 00:21:50,943
- One touch of the blade
and it opens and shuts

528
00:21:50,943 --> 00:21:54,347
floors, doors, walls
and portcullises.

529
00:21:54,347 --> 00:21:56,215
- [Joel] And its snapples caps
off jugs, bottles and jars.

530
00:21:56,215 --> 00:21:57,617
- Shuts them too, you say.

531
00:21:57,617 --> 00:21:59,418
- [Tom] What the hell.

532
00:22:00,987 --> 00:22:02,122
- What's down there?

533
00:22:02,122 --> 00:22:03,357
- [Tom] China.

534
00:22:03,357 --> 00:22:04,992
- I haven't been down
there in centuries.

535
00:22:04,992 --> 00:22:08,695
It used to be my brother's
safe deposit box storeroom.

536
00:22:08,695 --> 00:22:12,598
Spells, enchantments,
magic rituals and the like.

537
00:22:12,598 --> 00:22:14,100
Want to see?

538
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:15,968
- [Joel] Old magazines and
my high school yearbook.

539
00:22:15,968 --> 00:22:18,605
- Is there any other way out
if the crack were closed again?

540
00:22:18,605 --> 00:22:20,873
- [Crow] Well, there's
the kitchen door.

541
00:22:20,873 --> 00:22:24,878
- A cousin of mine took 80
years to work up a spell

542
00:22:24,878 --> 00:22:27,647
that blew the roof off, but...

543
00:22:27,647 --> 00:22:29,048
- [Tom] She's got more
stories about her relatives

544
00:22:29,048 --> 00:22:30,450
than Gabe Kaplan.

545
00:22:31,918 --> 00:22:33,353
- I'm not afraid.

546
00:22:34,955 --> 00:22:36,657
You go first, Mother.

547
00:22:38,925 --> 00:22:41,060
- [Tom] Age before
beauty, I guess.

548
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:43,297
Whoa, I didn't wanna see that.

549
00:22:43,297 --> 00:22:46,733
♪ One singular sensation ♪

550
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:55,008
- [Tom] Hey.

551
00:22:57,443 --> 00:22:59,212
(sword clanging)
- [Joel] Psych!

552
00:22:59,212 --> 00:23:00,080
- [Sybil] George!

553
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:01,615
- [Joel] My toe!

554
00:23:01,615 --> 00:23:04,117
- [Sybil] George, what have
you done? George, let me out.

555
00:23:04,117 --> 00:23:05,218
- Goodbye, Mother.

556
00:23:05,218 --> 00:23:06,318
- [Sybil] George!

557
00:23:06,318 --> 00:23:07,853
George, let me out this instant.

558
00:23:07,853 --> 00:23:10,823
You can't leave me here, I
told you about my cousin!

559
00:23:10,823 --> 00:23:12,558
- I'll come back and let you out

560
00:23:12,558 --> 00:23:14,995
after I've rescued
the princess Helene.

561
00:23:14,995 --> 00:23:17,430
- [Tom] But I'll
be hungry by then.

562
00:23:17,430 --> 00:23:19,967
- With the magic armor,
magic sword, magic steed.

563
00:23:19,967 --> 00:23:21,233
- [Crow] And my
refrigeration certificate

564
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:22,735
from Pine City Vo-Tech.

565
00:23:22,735 --> 00:23:24,370
- [Sybil] You don't know Lodac.

566
00:23:24,370 --> 00:23:26,607
George, George, let me out!

567
00:23:27,507 --> 00:23:30,510
- [Joel] (scoffing) Taffeta.

568
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:31,912
- [Tom] Let's go.

569
00:23:31,912 --> 00:23:33,078
- [Joel] Hey, Basil Rathbone,
that gives me an idea.

570
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:36,917
Remember those doggie
costumes we had?

571
00:23:36,917 --> 00:23:41,922
(mechanical whirring)
(doors closing)

572
00:23:47,427 --> 00:23:48,895
(bots whining and barking)

573
00:23:48,895 --> 00:23:51,197
You know, you get out of your
dog what you put into it.

574
00:23:51,197 --> 00:23:52,598
- [Magic Voice] Top
trainer, Joel Robinson.

575
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:56,068
- And I only put in the
best, Basil Rathbones.

576
00:23:56,068 --> 00:23:57,837
Okay, Crow, okay.

577
00:23:57,837 --> 00:24:00,140
Okay boy, wait for
it, wait for it..

578
00:24:00,140 --> 00:24:01,007
Good!

579
00:24:01,007 --> 00:24:02,208
(laughing)

580
00:24:02,208 --> 00:24:04,277
You know, a top-trained
dog like this one

581
00:24:04,277 --> 00:24:06,245
is a lot like any of us people.

582
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:09,282
You know, we all need
affection, occasional grooming

583
00:24:09,282 --> 00:24:11,785
and lots and lots of snacks.

584
00:24:11,785 --> 00:24:15,388
And dogs just go nuts for the
rich taste of Basil Rathbones.

585
00:24:15,388 --> 00:24:18,392
One Rathbone a day will
clean doggie's teeth

586
00:24:18,392 --> 00:24:20,027
and freshen doggie breath.

587
00:24:20,027 --> 00:24:21,928
- And they're packed
with bits of Nigel Bruce,

588
00:24:21,928 --> 00:24:24,297
- Hey, these are too
good to be good for you!

589
00:24:24,297 --> 00:24:26,567
- Okay Tom Servo, sit, sit.

590
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:29,702
Good doggie.

591
00:24:29,702 --> 00:24:32,605
(laughing) Basil Rathbones.

592
00:24:32,605 --> 00:24:34,740
- And pesto-flavored
Basil Rathbones,

593
00:24:34,740 --> 00:24:36,877
for the pretentious dog.

594
00:24:36,877 --> 00:24:38,478
- [Magic Voice] Now in
rice and stick flavor,

595
00:24:38,478 --> 00:24:40,347
- It's alimentary,
my dear Robinson

596
00:24:40,347 --> 00:24:42,615
, to love Basil Rathbones.

597
00:24:42,615 --> 00:24:45,618
- Have my doggies been good
on the Satellite of Love?

598
00:24:45,618 --> 00:24:47,387
Oh, they are such
good, good doggies.

599
00:24:47,387 --> 00:24:49,655
Do the doggies want
to go out and...

600
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:53,227
(instrumental theme music)

601
00:24:55,795 --> 00:24:58,298
(dramatic music)

602
00:24:58,298 --> 00:25:00,167
- [Crow] We bring you
tennis balls, your majesty.

603
00:25:00,167 --> 00:25:01,067
- [Tom] Woof.

604
00:25:01,067 --> 00:25:02,235
Got fur in my mouth.

605
00:25:02,235 --> 00:25:03,503
Your majesty,
these knights and I

606
00:25:03,503 --> 00:25:05,472
have come to serve you
in your hour of need.

607
00:25:05,472 --> 00:25:06,673
- That is very kind.

608
00:25:06,673 --> 00:25:08,275
- [Tom] But we're
not hiring right now.

609
00:25:08,275 --> 00:25:10,610
- I am Sir George, a
knight by virtue of

610
00:25:10,610 --> 00:25:12,578
400 years of noble lineage.

611
00:25:12,578 --> 00:25:15,148
- [Crow] And a degree from
Cardinal Stritch College.

612
00:25:15,148 --> 00:25:17,650
- These are my comrades in arms.

613
00:25:17,650 --> 00:25:19,285
Sir Dennis of France.

614
00:25:19,285 --> 00:25:20,520
- Your majesty--

615
00:25:20,520 --> 00:25:22,022
- [Joel] He's gonna have
really bad hat hair.

616
00:25:22,022 --> 00:25:23,223
- [Crow] Oh yeah.

617
00:25:23,223 --> 00:25:24,892
- [George] Sir
Ulrich of Germany.

618
00:25:24,892 --> 00:25:27,160
- Mein Keiser, we come to serve.

619
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:28,395
- [Joel] The voice
of Paul Frees.

620
00:25:28,395 --> 00:25:29,228
- [George] Sir Anthony of Italy.

621
00:25:29,228 --> 00:25:30,630
- [Tom] Yo, Tony!

622
00:25:32,565 --> 00:25:34,233
- [Joel] Harry Shearer.
- [George] Sir Pedro of Spain.

623
00:25:34,233 --> 00:25:37,670
- [Crow] He's got an
observatory on his head.

624
00:25:37,670 --> 00:25:39,672
- [George] Sir
James of Scotland.

625
00:25:39,672 --> 00:25:43,677
- Our hearts grieve for you
in your sorrow, your majesty.

626
00:25:43,677 --> 00:25:44,912
- [George] And last--

627
00:25:44,912 --> 00:25:46,847
- [Joel] Terry, the
sensitive knight.

628
00:25:46,847 --> 00:25:49,115
- We pledge our
lives to your service

629
00:25:49,115 --> 00:25:51,718
and to the princess
Helene until she's safe.

630
00:25:51,718 --> 00:25:53,487
- [Crow] What, is he the
knight from the Bronx?

631
00:25:53,487 --> 00:25:56,657
- Speaking for the king, we
are grateful for your offer.

632
00:25:56,657 --> 00:25:58,425
I am sure that you can be
of immeasurable service

633
00:25:58,425 --> 00:26:00,793
to his majesty while I'm away.

634
00:26:00,793 --> 00:26:03,563
- [Tom] We'll keep
your resumes on file.

635
00:26:03,563 --> 00:26:05,198
- Oh, you know who I am.

636
00:26:05,198 --> 00:26:06,298
Have we met?

637
00:26:06,298 --> 00:26:08,435
- [Crow] That's an old line.

638
00:26:08,435 --> 00:26:09,568
- In the field?

639
00:26:09,568 --> 00:26:11,070
- Not in the field.

640
00:26:11,070 --> 00:26:13,340
And I also know you wish to
marry the princess Helene.

641
00:26:13,340 --> 00:26:14,840
- Quite true.

642
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:17,110
You're all welcome to stay
and dance at my wedding.

643
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:18,210
- [Tom] Yeah, me and what army?

644
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,245
Oh.
- Many thanks,

645
00:26:19,245 --> 00:26:21,113
but I prefer to dance at my own.

646
00:26:21,113 --> 00:26:23,750
- [Crow] Uh, we're getting
into a weird area here.

647
00:26:23,750 --> 00:26:24,985
- Don't try to solve them until

648
00:26:24,985 --> 00:26:26,920
we've rescued the
princess Helene.

649
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:28,153
- We?

650
00:26:28,153 --> 00:26:31,257
- [Joel] What do you
mean we, Kemosabe?

651
00:26:31,257 --> 00:26:33,258
- Monsieur, try to understand.

652
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:37,163
We are all sworn to save
Sir George's beautiful lady.

653
00:26:37,163 --> 00:26:39,165
- [Tom] I think what our
bright young French friend

654
00:26:39,165 --> 00:26:41,433
is trying to say is...

655
00:26:41,433 --> 00:26:43,803
- What does the Frenchman mean?

656
00:26:43,803 --> 00:26:46,305
- Only that I love her
and I intend to marry her.

657
00:26:46,305 --> 00:26:47,140
- [Tom] Oh okay--

658
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:47,973
Hey!

659
00:26:49,108 --> 00:26:51,110
- Do you know the perils
of the dark journey?

660
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:52,478
- We do, Sir Branton.

661
00:26:52,478 --> 00:26:53,980
If you don't share
our enthusiasm,

662
00:26:53,980 --> 00:26:55,482
we shall be happy to
go on without you.

663
00:26:55,482 --> 00:26:57,883
- [Joel] Ha ha ha huh?

664
00:26:57,883 --> 00:26:59,518
- Your majesty, have I
your permission to give

665
00:26:59,518 --> 00:27:01,520
this stripling a lesson
in the use of arms?

666
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:03,155
- [Crow] Permission to
cut him ib half, sir!

667
00:27:03,155 --> 00:27:04,123
- I shall not draw.

668
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:05,425
- [Tom] I shall paint.

669
00:27:05,425 --> 00:27:07,393
- Except on behalf
of Princess Helene.

670
00:27:07,393 --> 00:27:08,762
- A coward.

671
00:27:08,762 --> 00:27:09,595
Draw.

672
00:27:11,397 --> 00:27:12,765
(sword clanging)

673
00:27:12,765 --> 00:27:14,533
- [Joel] Jerk, you
broke my sword!

674
00:27:14,533 --> 00:27:16,535
(crowd murmuring)

675
00:27:16,535 --> 00:27:18,438
- Enough, that's enough!

676
00:27:18,438 --> 00:27:21,440
Sir Branton, I
like these knights.

677
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,443
- [Crow] You violated ape law.

678
00:27:23,443 --> 00:27:26,578
- You and seven good swords.

679
00:27:26,578 --> 00:27:27,613
- Seven swords.

680
00:27:27,613 --> 00:27:29,482
- [Tom] For seven brothers.

681
00:27:29,482 --> 00:27:30,617
- Seven curses.

682
00:27:30,617 --> 00:27:32,118
- [Tom] For seven brothers.

683
00:27:32,118 --> 00:27:34,520
- When do we start, Sir Branton?

684
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:35,755
- Now.

685
00:27:35,755 --> 00:27:37,623
- [Crow] On your
mark, get set, go!

686
00:27:37,623 --> 00:27:38,692
- [Joel] Hi-keeba.

687
00:27:38,692 --> 00:27:40,360
(frustrated grumbling)

688
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:43,497
- [Tom] And a double hi-keeba.

689
00:27:43,497 --> 00:27:45,332
I just raised him one.

690
00:27:46,532 --> 00:27:49,935
♪ Knights in white satin ♪

691
00:27:52,672 --> 00:27:56,943
- [Tom] Come on, you
ragtag bunch of misfits.

692
00:27:56,943 --> 00:27:59,312
- [Crow] Whew, glad I don't
jave to mow that lawn.

693
00:27:59,312 --> 00:28:02,048
- [Tom] Looks like
a golf course.

694
00:28:05,752 --> 00:28:07,820
- [Joel] Tonight on Mime Court.

695
00:28:07,820 --> 00:28:09,088
- [Crow] If you're really bad,

696
00:28:09,088 --> 00:28:11,623
they throw you in
the imaginary box.

697
00:28:12,692 --> 00:28:14,427
- [Joel] Petticoat Dungeon.

698
00:28:14,427 --> 00:28:15,528
- I'm Helene.

699
00:28:16,930 --> 00:28:19,665
- We know, we heard you were
brought in this morning.

700
00:28:19,665 --> 00:28:22,802
I'm Princess Laura, and
this is my sister Grace.

701
00:28:22,802 --> 00:28:24,303
This is our seventh day.

702
00:28:24,303 --> 00:28:26,405
- [Crow] Let's
form a girl group.

703
00:28:26,405 --> 00:28:28,975
- Our last day, unless...

704
00:28:28,975 --> 00:28:32,112
- Surely you don't believe
that about the dragon.

705
00:28:32,112 --> 00:28:33,947
- There were others
here when we arrived,

706
00:28:33,947 --> 00:28:35,248
but they're gone now.

707
00:28:35,248 --> 00:28:36,750
- [Tom] Georgette, everybody.

708
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:39,418
- Then your father will
do something to save you.

709
00:28:39,418 --> 00:28:40,820
Why, his army is probably

710
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:42,788
approaching the castle
this very minute.

711
00:28:42,788 --> 00:28:44,157
- [Joel] Don't kid
yourself, sister.

712
00:28:44,157 --> 00:28:46,793
We've been here for seven years.

713
00:28:46,793 --> 00:28:49,362
- You'll be on your
way home by morning.

714
00:28:49,362 --> 00:28:50,763
(roaring)

715
00:28:50,763 --> 00:28:52,532
- [Crow] Uh, that's my dad.

716
00:28:52,532 --> 00:28:54,700
(roaring)

717
00:29:01,340 --> 00:29:02,608
- The two sisters.

718
00:29:02,608 --> 00:29:05,178
♪ There were never
such devoted sisters ♪

719
00:29:05,178 --> 00:29:06,378
- [Crow] Eraserhead.

720
00:29:06,378 --> 00:29:08,213
- [Joel] Literally.
- Are we to go home now,

721
00:29:08,213 --> 00:29:10,817
has Father arranged
for our release?

722
00:29:10,817 --> 00:29:12,352
- You're not going home.

723
00:29:12,352 --> 00:29:13,520
- [Crow] You're
going to Disneyland.

724
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:15,155
- Surely you've spoken to him?

725
00:29:15,155 --> 00:29:18,492
- I've had three long,
dull sessions with him

726
00:29:18,492 --> 00:29:21,293
but nothing could persuade him
to give up what I asked for.

727
00:29:21,293 --> 00:29:24,297
- I don't believe you,
he'd pay you anything!

728
00:29:24,297 --> 00:29:25,798
- Nothing.

729
00:29:25,798 --> 00:29:27,333
Instead, he sent
an entire company

730
00:29:27,333 --> 00:29:30,903
of his bravest knights
on the dark journey.

731
00:29:30,903 --> 00:29:34,040
The poor lads never even
reached the third curse.

732
00:29:34,040 --> 00:29:35,073
Take them away.

733
00:29:35,073 --> 00:29:36,142
- [Joel] They bore me.

734
00:29:36,142 --> 00:29:37,777
(princesses screaming)

735
00:29:37,777 --> 00:29:39,278
- [Crow] Can I take their
Snoopy poster down now?

736
00:29:39,278 --> 00:29:42,648
- This just can't be happening.

737
00:29:42,648 --> 00:29:44,150
There just couldn't be anybody

738
00:29:44,150 --> 00:29:46,953
as cruel and evil as you.
- [Tom] No, I won't hear it!

739
00:29:46,953 --> 00:29:48,187
There's a man in Eastbourne.

740
00:29:48,187 --> 00:29:49,422
- You think this
is the first time

741
00:29:49,422 --> 00:29:51,157
that a princess has
been fed to a dragon?

742
00:29:51,157 --> 00:29:53,693
At least around here it
happens only once a week.

743
00:29:53,693 --> 00:29:55,695
- Unless you get what you want.

744
00:29:55,695 --> 00:29:57,530
What ransom are
you asking for me?

745
00:29:57,530 --> 00:29:59,965
- I'm sorry, but you happen
to be a particular case.

746
00:29:59,965 --> 00:30:02,768
I'm not asking any
ransom for you at all.

747
00:30:02,768 --> 00:30:04,503
- Then why did
you bring me here?

748
00:30:04,503 --> 00:30:08,340
- My little pet will be hungry
again in six days' time.

749
00:30:08,340 --> 00:30:10,943
(roaring)
- [Crow] Uh, five days' time.

750
00:30:10,943 --> 00:30:12,278
- No, no please.

751
00:30:13,145 --> 00:30:14,713
No, please.

752
00:30:14,713 --> 00:30:16,515
- [Joel] Is she soup yet?

753
00:30:16,515 --> 00:30:18,150
- [Tom] Mmm, mmm, dead.

754
00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:20,018
- The wind carries well.

755
00:30:20,018 --> 00:30:23,923
Don't turn your head away,
you'll miss all the fun.

756
00:30:23,923 --> 00:30:24,923
You see?

757
00:30:24,923 --> 00:30:26,092
- [Crow] Ah, he does light cues.

758
00:30:26,092 --> 00:30:28,528
- It happens very quickly.

759
00:30:28,528 --> 00:30:30,497
Now my little pet can sleep.

760
00:30:30,497 --> 00:30:32,365
- It's horrible.

761
00:30:32,365 --> 00:30:34,000
- [Joel] Oh bite me, it's fun.

762
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,968
- But it won't happen to me.

763
00:30:35,968 --> 00:30:37,603
Their father sent a company.

764
00:30:37,603 --> 00:30:39,338
Well mine will send an army!

765
00:30:39,338 --> 00:30:40,873
- [Tom] My Westley
will come for me.

766
00:30:40,873 --> 00:30:43,075
- I hate to disillusion you.

767
00:30:43,075 --> 00:30:46,012
Actually, for a while,
your father seemed content

768
00:30:46,012 --> 00:30:49,782
to let just one knight
undertake your rescue.

769
00:30:49,782 --> 00:30:51,683
Oh, don't blame your father.

770
00:30:51,683 --> 00:30:53,787
The knight talked him into it.

771
00:30:53,787 --> 00:30:55,888
- And who is this
very brave knight?

772
00:30:55,888 --> 00:30:57,023
- I'm sure you know him.

773
00:30:57,023 --> 00:30:57,857
- [Joel] Murray.
- Sir Branton.

774
00:30:57,857 --> 00:30:59,892
- [Joel] Sir Frampton?

775
00:30:59,892 --> 00:31:01,027
- Sir Branton.

776
00:31:01,027 --> 00:31:02,128
- [Tom] Oh, he's a freshman.

777
00:31:02,128 --> 00:31:03,295
- You don't like Sir Branton?

778
00:31:03,295 --> 00:31:04,897
Oh, come now.

779
00:31:04,897 --> 00:31:08,367
A damsel in distress can't
afford to pick and choose.

780
00:31:08,367 --> 00:31:09,868
Anyway, don't worry.

781
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:12,672
Neither he nor his companions
will ever get here.

782
00:31:12,672 --> 00:31:15,575
- Companions, I thought you
said Sir Branton was alone.

783
00:31:15,575 --> 00:31:19,645
- He would have been, but
some foolhardy young man

784
00:31:19,645 --> 00:31:22,248
named George insisted
on coming with him.

785
00:31:22,248 --> 00:31:23,082
- George?

786
00:31:24,283 --> 00:31:25,518
- [Lodac] Of course,
you don't know him.

787
00:31:25,518 --> 00:31:26,485
- [Joel] You don't
know him, he's new.

788
00:31:26,485 --> 00:31:28,353
- Where is he?

789
00:31:28,353 --> 00:31:29,755
- Would you care to see him?

790
00:31:29,755 --> 00:31:32,458
- [Crow] Feel him, touch him?

791
00:31:32,458 --> 00:31:35,962
- Certainly, I'll show
you the young fool.

792
00:31:39,998 --> 00:31:41,500
- [Tom] It's pay-per-view,
we can only watch it

793
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:43,368
for two minutes
before they charge us.

794
00:31:43,368 --> 00:31:45,103
- Which one is George?

795
00:31:45,103 --> 00:31:46,872
- The youngest.

796
00:31:46,872 --> 00:31:50,343
He's in the lead,
riding with Sir Branton.

797
00:31:52,945 --> 00:31:55,715
- [Joel] Boy, that place
could use some yardwork.

798
00:31:55,715 --> 00:31:59,352
- [Tom] Looks like
Cypress Gardens, Florida.

799
00:32:00,587 --> 00:32:02,688
- Those who are wise
will turn back now.

800
00:32:02,688 --> 00:32:05,558
- [Tom] Okay, see ya.
- Bye, thanks.

801
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:09,495
- [Crow] Hah, they're
riding carousel horses

802
00:32:09,495 --> 00:32:11,063
like Marry Poppins.

803
00:32:12,732 --> 00:32:16,335
(instrumental theme music)

804
00:32:21,573 --> 00:32:24,310
- [Tom] Look, that
guy hit a bug.

805
00:32:26,112 --> 00:32:29,348
- [Crow] Oh, we're
back, nothing there.

806
00:32:31,683 --> 00:32:33,518
- [Joel] It's a K.O.A.

807
00:32:36,322 --> 00:32:40,225
- [Tom] You guys cower
over here, I'll go look.

808
00:32:43,730 --> 00:32:46,665
- [Crow] Oh, let
me see this thing.

809
00:32:48,367 --> 00:32:51,870
- [Tom] Huh?
(growling)

810
00:32:51,870 --> 00:32:54,040
- [Joel] Teddy Ruxpin, no!

811
00:32:57,010 --> 00:32:58,310
(growling)

812
00:32:58,310 --> 00:33:01,413
- [Tom] Kinda looks
like Gino Vannelli.

813
00:33:01,413 --> 00:33:03,615
(growling)

814
00:33:09,622 --> 00:33:10,657
- [Tom] Ouch.

815
00:33:12,492 --> 00:33:14,993
- [Crow] Sanctuary, sanctuary!

816
00:33:16,195 --> 00:33:18,630
- [Tom] Sanctuary
much. (chuckling)

817
00:33:18,630 --> 00:33:22,135
Think that hurts,
look at this perm!

818
00:33:22,135 --> 00:33:24,670
- [Joel] It's Ron Perlman.

819
00:33:24,670 --> 00:33:26,305
- [Crow] Ah shoot,
this is real fur!

820
00:33:26,305 --> 00:33:28,975
You know how hard it
is to get blood out?

821
00:33:28,975 --> 00:33:31,243
(growling)

822
00:33:36,082 --> 00:33:37,917
- [Tom] It's a salted nut log.

823
00:33:37,917 --> 00:33:40,853
Captain's log. (chuckling)

824
00:33:40,853 --> 00:33:42,455
- [Joel] That's his
only move, essentially.

825
00:33:42,455 --> 00:33:43,288
- [Crow] Yeah.

826
00:33:43,288 --> 00:33:45,323
- [Tom] Pretty much.

827
00:33:45,323 --> 00:33:47,893
- [Crow] All right,
anyone know what that is?

828
00:33:47,893 --> 00:33:49,395
- Keep back always, he's mine.

829
00:33:49,395 --> 00:33:50,663
- [Tom] He's yours?

830
00:33:50,663 --> 00:33:53,900
Then tell him to stop
throwing stuff at us!

831
00:33:53,900 --> 00:33:56,335
- [Joel] We talked about it
and we'd really appreciate it

832
00:33:56,335 --> 00:33:58,838
if you'd stop throwing things.

833
00:34:01,607 --> 00:34:02,875
- [Tom] Yeah, it's over
by the Seven-Eleven

834
00:34:02,875 --> 00:34:06,345
and you take a left,
okay, by the freeway.

835
00:34:09,115 --> 00:34:10,850
- [Crow] Heh-heh, it's
a troll in the hay!

836
00:34:10,850 --> 00:34:11,817
- [Tom] D'oh!

837
00:34:11,817 --> 00:34:13,385
- [Joel] Literally.

838
00:34:17,123 --> 00:34:20,727
- [Tom] Kinda looks like
Barry Gibb, doesn't he?

839
00:34:20,727 --> 00:34:25,732
- [Joel] Have some pumpernickel
bread with me, friend, here.

840
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:28,633
- [Crow] Stop, that's
no way to kill roaches.

841
00:34:28,633 --> 00:34:31,070
- [Tom] Now he's
throwing beefsteak rye.

842
00:34:31,070 --> 00:34:32,572
Sure is hearty.

843
00:34:32,572 --> 00:34:36,875
- [Joel] Ah, I gotta learn
to lead that little guy.

844
00:34:36,875 --> 00:34:40,580
♪ Round round, get around,
I get around yeah ♪

845
00:34:40,580 --> 00:34:42,582
- [Crow] Goofy, isn't it?

846
00:34:42,582 --> 00:34:43,850
- That horse is swift.

847
00:34:43,850 --> 00:34:45,485
- [Tom] It's a pilot,
so it's an hour long.

848
00:34:45,485 --> 00:34:47,320
- No, no, no, no.

849
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:49,188
Just a stupid thought
that crossed my mind.

850
00:34:49,188 --> 00:34:51,157
- [Tom] I thought maybe you
and I could, oh never mind.

851
00:34:51,157 --> 00:34:52,992
- My ogre will kill them both.

852
00:34:52,992 --> 00:34:54,160
- [Crow] His odor?

853
00:34:54,160 --> 00:34:56,128
- Are you quite sure?

854
00:34:56,128 --> 00:35:01,133
- [Tom] He needs Ogre
Eaters. (laughing)

855
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,568
- [Joel] I am not an animal.

856
00:35:06,705 --> 00:35:10,075
- [Crow] Look out,
he's gonna launch!

857
00:35:10,075 --> 00:35:11,577
- [Tom] He's kinda got Conway
Twitty hair doesn't he?

858
00:35:11,577 --> 00:35:12,878
- [Joel] Mm-hmm.

859
00:35:12,878 --> 00:35:15,882
- [Crow] Watch this,
kinda pathetic.

860
00:35:16,815 --> 00:35:18,450
- [Joel] Ga-nish!

861
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:19,785
- [Tom] Ga-nish?

862
00:35:21,253 --> 00:35:24,523
- [Crow] Ya got me. (groaning)

863
00:35:24,523 --> 00:35:26,425
- [Tom] Chest Hair
Club, for men.

864
00:35:26,425 --> 00:35:28,293
(yelling)

865
00:35:28,293 --> 00:35:30,630
- [Joel] Yeah, I'm gonna
make him into a fort!

866
00:35:30,630 --> 00:35:32,598
(bots cheering)

867
00:35:32,598 --> 00:35:33,632
- He's won!

868
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:35,267
He beat you at your own game.

869
00:35:35,267 --> 00:35:36,435
- So he did.

870
00:35:36,435 --> 00:35:37,570
- [Tom] Now where's
my ten bucks?

871
00:35:37,570 --> 00:35:39,338
- He'll save me, I know he will.

872
00:35:39,338 --> 00:35:41,073
- Not a chance.

873
00:35:41,073 --> 00:35:43,977
No one has ever survived
the seven curses of Lodac.

874
00:35:43,977 --> 00:35:45,077
That was only the first.

875
00:35:45,077 --> 00:35:46,578
- [Joel] Now it's six curses!

876
00:35:46,578 --> 00:35:49,182
- [Crow] Shut up, shut up!

877
00:35:49,182 --> 00:35:53,318
- [Tom] He's evil, but he
should spat more, you know?

878
00:35:53,318 --> 00:35:54,453
- [Joel] They buried him?

879
00:35:54,453 --> 00:35:55,955
- And still not a sign of our

880
00:35:55,955 --> 00:35:57,923
gallant commander, Sir Branton.

881
00:35:57,923 --> 00:35:59,992
- [Crow] You make me
sick, you stupid pig.

882
00:35:59,992 --> 00:36:02,195
- Not to pay respect
when poor Ulrich

883
00:36:02,195 --> 00:36:04,497
and Pedro are laid to rest.

884
00:36:04,497 --> 00:36:06,632
- But is the man a
coward, not to have

885
00:36:06,632 --> 00:36:09,168
lifted his sword
against that monster?

886
00:36:09,168 --> 00:36:10,435
- Branton's no coward.

887
00:36:10,435 --> 00:36:13,940
- [Crow] They're praying
over the monster's butt.

888
00:36:13,940 --> 00:36:16,042
- We missed you at the
burial, Sir Branton.

889
00:36:16,042 --> 00:36:17,643
- [Joel] Don't say hi.

890
00:36:17,643 --> 00:36:20,078
- My regrets, gentlemen,
are as deep as your own,

891
00:36:20,078 --> 00:36:23,582
but since every minute
counts, I thought it wiser

892
00:36:23,582 --> 00:36:25,217
for me to ride ahead
and reconnoiter.

893
00:36:25,217 --> 00:36:27,987
(Tom imitates chicken clucking)

894
00:36:27,987 --> 00:36:29,455
- Mount your horses, gentlemen.

895
00:36:29,455 --> 00:36:30,522
- [Crow] We're not that lonely!

896
00:36:30,522 --> 00:36:31,923
- And come see for yourselves.

897
00:36:31,923 --> 00:36:34,927
- [Joel] Yeah, let's
get outta here.

898
00:36:37,363 --> 00:36:39,098
The mists of Avalon.

899
00:36:39,098 --> 00:36:41,800
♪ Avalon ♪

900
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:42,735
- [Tom] This is a hair follicle

901
00:36:42,735 --> 00:36:45,203
magnifiedúover a million times.

902
00:36:46,372 --> 00:36:47,607
- [Joel] You know,
I was just thinking

903
00:36:47,607 --> 00:36:48,873
this is really pretty
good for a Bert I...

904
00:36:48,873 --> 00:36:50,142
- [Crow] What!?

905
00:36:51,310 --> 00:36:52,812
- [Tom] Well yeah,
for Bert I. Gordon.

906
00:36:52,812 --> 00:36:53,645
- [Crow] Well...

907
00:36:53,645 --> 00:36:55,513
♪ I get misty ♪

908
00:36:55,513 --> 00:36:58,583
♪ Smoke gets in your eyes ♪

909
00:36:58,583 --> 00:37:00,385
♪ Smoke on the ♪

910
00:37:00,385 --> 00:37:01,720
- [Crow] Oh, for
cryin' out loud!

911
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:04,623
(laughing)

912
00:37:04,623 --> 00:37:05,758
♪ On top of Old Smokey ♪

913
00:37:05,758 --> 00:37:06,892
- [Crow] Okay.

914
00:37:06,892 --> 00:37:09,828
- [Joel] Hollywood Hot Tubs Two.

915
00:37:09,828 --> 00:37:11,430
- [Tom] Really makes
ya think, don't it?

916
00:37:11,430 --> 00:37:12,598
- [Joel] Nope.

917
00:37:13,967 --> 00:37:15,635
(water bubbling)

918
00:37:15,635 --> 00:37:18,170
- [Tom] Just what I mean,
I was trying to think of

919
00:37:18,170 --> 00:37:20,138
something to say, I mean we're
supposed to be on a quest.

920
00:37:20,138 --> 00:37:21,640
We're supposed to
be best friends,

921
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:23,175
we haven't even talked yet.

922
00:37:23,175 --> 00:37:24,410
- [Joel] We've talked.

923
00:37:24,410 --> 00:37:25,645
- [Tom] No, no, I
mean really talked.

924
00:37:25,645 --> 00:37:26,678
All I know about you
is that you're French.

925
00:37:26,678 --> 00:37:28,513
France is a big country and all.

926
00:37:28,513 --> 00:37:29,748
- [Joel] Not really.

927
00:37:29,748 --> 00:37:31,750
- [Crow] Are we in
the Renaissance?

928
00:37:31,750 --> 00:37:33,987
- [Joel] No, no, we're
in the early Middle Ages.

929
00:37:33,987 --> 00:37:35,187
- [Crow] How do you know?

930
00:37:35,187 --> 00:37:36,455
- [Joel] Well, take
the distinction

931
00:37:36,455 --> 00:37:37,757
between the slave
and the free man.

932
00:37:37,757 --> 00:37:38,723
- [Crow] What about it?

933
00:37:38,723 --> 00:37:39,625
- [Joel] Well, it's weakening.

934
00:37:39,625 --> 00:37:41,127
- [Crow] Oh.

935
00:37:41,127 --> 00:37:42,428
- [Tom] You know, even if
we were in the Renaissance,

936
00:37:42,428 --> 00:37:45,563
how would we know we
were in the Renaissance?

937
00:37:45,563 --> 00:37:46,832
- [Knight] Would you
look at that, George?

938
00:37:46,832 --> 00:37:47,933
- [Crow] Wow.

939
00:37:49,035 --> 00:37:50,737
It's a virtual bloodbath.

940
00:37:50,737 --> 00:37:52,305
- [Joel] Literally.

941
00:37:53,505 --> 00:37:54,740
- [Tom] This may be a quest,

942
00:37:54,740 --> 00:37:57,242
but it's also kind
of fun isn't it?

943
00:37:58,577 --> 00:38:00,680
- This would be an unsavory
region, Sir Branton.

944
00:38:00,680 --> 00:38:04,883
- [Crow] So fair and foul
a day I have not seen.

945
00:38:04,883 --> 00:38:07,320
- Why, it isn't a
road we're on at all.

946
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,288
The fog's getting thicker.

947
00:38:09,288 --> 00:38:10,222
Where's Dennis?

948
00:38:10,222 --> 00:38:11,323
- [Joel] At Mr. Wilson's?

949
00:38:11,323 --> 00:38:14,360
- Where's James and Anthony?

950
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:15,527
James, Dennis!

951
00:38:16,695 --> 00:38:17,530
Anthony!

952
00:38:20,667 --> 00:38:22,602
- [Tom] I say it's a bit foggy!

953
00:38:22,602 --> 00:38:24,870
- Well then keep
with us, keep close!

954
00:38:24,870 --> 00:38:26,872
- [Crow] And keep
reaching for the stars~

955
00:38:26,872 --> 00:38:28,207
- [Knight] Where's Anthony?

956
00:38:28,207 --> 00:38:29,375
Anthony!

957
00:38:29,375 --> 00:38:30,910
- [Joel] It's Prince
spaghetti day!

958
00:38:30,910 --> 00:38:33,212
- [Knight] Anthony!

959
00:38:33,212 --> 00:38:34,413
Anthony!

960
00:38:34,413 --> 00:38:37,517
- [Tom] Nothing, I'm
just playing over here!

961
00:38:37,517 --> 00:38:40,887
- [Joel] This is a hair
follicle after being blow-dried.

962
00:38:40,887 --> 00:38:43,088
- [Knight] Anthony!

963
00:38:43,088 --> 00:38:45,023
- [Crow] Look,
Anthony's gone, okay?

964
00:38:45,023 --> 00:38:49,695
(Joel and Tom imitating
jungle animals)

965
00:38:50,863 --> 00:38:52,230
- [Knight] Anthony!

966
00:38:52,230 --> 00:38:53,498
- [Joel] Zerbe!

967
00:38:55,735 --> 00:38:57,470
- [Knight] Which way are you?

968
00:38:57,470 --> 00:38:59,105
- Here!

969
00:38:59,105 --> 00:39:02,942
- [Crow] I'm over here
in the hydrangea bush!

970
00:39:02,942 --> 00:39:05,043
- [Tom] Strider, Boromir!

971
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:11,650
- [Joel] It's Dean Jones
in The Love Knight, ha ha.

972
00:39:11,650 --> 00:39:14,320
(screaming)

973
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,253
- Find him!

974
00:39:23,028 --> 00:39:24,763
- Anthony, where are you?

975
00:39:24,763 --> 00:39:27,833
- [Crow] Now I am
over here drowning!

976
00:39:30,468 --> 00:39:31,303
- Where are you?

977
00:39:31,303 --> 00:39:32,237
- [Anthony] I'm here!

978
00:39:32,237 --> 00:39:33,705
- [Tom] Uh, I need specifics.

979
00:39:33,705 --> 00:39:35,340
Exactly what does here mean?

980
00:39:35,340 --> 00:39:37,410
- I'm being pulled under.

981
00:39:38,843 --> 00:39:39,878
- Give me your hand.

982
00:39:39,878 --> 00:39:42,648
(all applauding)
- [Joel] Yay.

983
00:39:42,648 --> 00:39:43,615
- Give me your hand.

984
00:39:43,615 --> 00:39:48,087
- [Joel] Okay!
(all applauding)

985
00:39:48,087 --> 00:39:51,823
You just ate, get out
of there, quit clowning.

986
00:39:51,823 --> 00:39:53,825
- [Crow] My beard's coming off.

987
00:39:53,825 --> 00:39:55,762
How you two doing over
here, everything okay?

988
00:39:55,762 --> 00:39:56,828
Ah, carry on.

989
00:40:00,265 --> 00:40:05,203
- [Joel] Hmm, his torso's gone,
he's been eaten by piranha!

990
00:40:08,640 --> 00:40:10,977
- [Tom] Have a nice
trip, see you next fall.

